Package: RADdiversity
Title: Population Genetic Statistics from RAD-Seq Data
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Nathan", "Whelan", email = "nathan.whelan@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Population-genetic summary statistics from RAD-seq data,
    designed around 'Stacks' 2 'populations' VCF output. Computes observed
    and expected heterozygosity (Nei and Chesser (1983)
    <doi:10.1111/j.1469-1809.1983.tb00993.x>), FIS as a ratio of sums,
    rarefied allelic and private allelic richness (Kalinowski (2004)
    <doi:10.1023/B:COGE.0000041021.91777.1a>), per-sequenced-site
    heterozygosity (Schmidt et al. (2021) <doi:10.1111/2041-210X.13659>),
    and Weir and Cockerham (1984) <doi:10.1111/j.1558-5646.1984.tb05657.x>
    FST and Jost (2008) <doi:10.1111/j.1365-294X.2008.03887.x> D, with block
    jackknife standard errors and block bootstrap confidence intervals over
    RAD loci. Tests whether populations differ in heterozygosity using the
    individual, not the locus, as the unit of replication. Also provides
    locus and genotype filters, an exact Hardy-Weinberg test, a kinship
    screen, and export to 'PLINK', 'STRUCTURE', 'Genepop', 'FSTAT',
    'RADpainter' and VCF formats.
